message: "If you use this knowledge engine or its curated dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "African Battery Materials Knowledge Engine: evidence-grounded literature mining, knowledge graph and hypothesis generation for AHSC and LLZO"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "michaelTomiwa"
    website: "https://github.com/michaelTomiwa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/michaelTomiwa/ahsc-llzo-analysis"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
keywords:
  - materials informatics
  - knowledge graph
  - large language models
  - GraphRAG
  - hypothesis generation
  - supercapacitors
  - LLZO
  - solid-state batteries
  - Africa
abstract: >-
  An LLM-powered knowledge engine that ingests battery-materials literature, extracts structured
  material-property-value facts with verbatim evidence grounding, constructs a knowledge graph, and
  generates testable hypotheses under African supply, energy and application constraints. It is
  validated on 533 manually curated literature records for asymmetric hybrid supercapacitors (AHSC)
  and garnet Li7La3Zr2O12 (LLZO) solid electrolytes.
